WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
Marcus signs an application and pays an initial premium.

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.800
Has he automatically received every benefit he requested?

3
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.600
Not necessarily. A valid contract needs agreement, consideration, competent

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.100
parties and a legal purpose.

5
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.180
The application commonly constitutes an offer, and the insurer decides

6
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.960
whether to accept under its rules.

7
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.360
If it offers different coverage or a higher premium, that may

8
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.160
be a counteroffer requiring acceptance.

9
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.860
The precise effective date also depends on the application, receipt and

10
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.220
policy conditions. A signature or payment alone is not a universal

11
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.634
coverage rule. Consideration is the value exchanged for

12
00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:42.774
the contractual promise. The applicant supplies the premium and application

13
00:00:42.774 --> 00:00:47.834
statements; the insurer supplies its promise to pay according

14
00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:52.694
to the contract. Competent parties must have the legal capacity to

15
00:00:52.694 --> 00:00:57.734
contract. A lawful purpose means the arrangement cannot be built around

16
00:00:57.734 --> 00:01:03.214
an illegal objective. Life insurance on another person also raises

17
00:01:03.214 --> 00:01:05.774
insurable-interest and consent requirements.

18
00:01:06.914 --> 00:01:09.454
These ideas are related but different.

19
00:01:10.474 --> 00:01:14.654
A perfectly completed form cannot make an illegal betting arrangement valid

20
00:01:14.654 --> 00:01:17.114
merely because someone paid a premium.

21
00:01:17.774 --> 00:01:22.954
Insurance is commonly described as a contract of adhesion because the

22
00:01:22.954 --> 00:01:28.014
insurer prepares the standard terms and the applicant generally

23
00:01:28.014 --> 00:01:30.154
accepts or rejects them.

24
00:01:30.854 --> 00:01:33.594
That does not mean a clear exclusion disappears.

25
00:01:34.854 --> 00:01:36.674
We will study interpretation separately.

26
00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:42.874
The contract is also aleatory: the value exchanged depends on

27
00:01:42.874 --> 00:01:45.794
an uncertain event and may be unequal.

28
00:01:46.494 --> 00:01:50.634
Marcus could pay a relatively small amount before a covered death

29
00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:52.794
produces a large benefit.

30
00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:56.814
Another insured may pay premiums for many years without a death

31
00:01:56.814 --> 00:01:59.494
claim during a term policy's coverage period.

32
00:02:00.344 --> 00:02:04.264
A life policy is usually described as unilateral because the insurer

33
00:02:04.264 --> 00:02:07.044
makes the enforceable promise to pay covered benefits.

34
00:02:07.564 --> 00:02:10.924
The owner can generally stop paying future premiums, subject to policy

35
00:02:10.924 --> 00:02:13.544
consequences such as lapse or use of available values.

36
00:02:13.924 --> 00:02:15.664
This does not mean the policy has no conditions.

37
00:02:16.364 --> 00:02:19.984
Coverage may depend on required premiums, truthful application information

38
00:02:19.984 --> 00:02:21.404
and other valid terms.

39
00:02:21.924 --> 00:02:24.544
Unilateral identifies the contractual promise.

40
00:02:24.924 --> 00:02:28.464
Conditional reminds you that the promise operates under specified

41
00:02:28.464 --> 00:02:32.784
requirements. Do not mistake either word for an unconditional promise to

42
00:02:32.784 --> 00:02:37.802
pay every claim. Indemnity generally aims to compensate an actual covered

43
00:02:37.802 --> 00:02:40.982
financial loss without creating a profit from that loss.

44
00:02:41.782 --> 00:02:46.562
Life insurance ordinarily pays a stated contractual death benefit rather than

45
00:02:46.562 --> 00:02:49.022
measuring the person's economic worth after death.

46
00:02:49.662 --> 00:02:53.322
The family does not submit every future household expense to set

47
00:02:53.322 --> 00:02:58.382
that amount. The personal-contract concept also needs care: many

48
00:02:58.382 --> 00:03:03.302
insurance contracts closely connect coverage to a particular insured risk,

49
00:03:03.942 --> 00:03:08.482
but life policies generally permit assignment of ownership rights under their

50
00:03:08.482 --> 00:03:10.582
terms and applicable law.

51
00:03:11.382 --> 00:03:14.682
Assignment does not change which person's life is insured.

52
00:03:15.668 --> 00:03:20.388
Suppose an applicant requests one rate, but the insurer offers a

53
00:03:20.388 --> 00:03:22.948
higher rate based on underwriting.

54
00:03:24.708 --> 00:03:30.268
Identify the counteroffer and the applicant's response before assuming

55
00:03:30.268 --> 00:03:32.648
a contract on the original terms.

56
00:03:33.808 --> 00:03:38.988
Then check the consideration, legal capacity and lawful purpose.

57
00:03:39.888 --> 00:03:43.600
Finally, apply the policy's conditions.

58
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:47.528
The exam may ask only for a characteristic, such

59
00:03:47.528 --> 00:03:52.668
as aleatory or adhesion, but a real file

60
00:03:52.668 --> 00:03:54.688
can involve several at once.

61
00:03:55.688 --> 00:04:01.088
Learn the reason each term fits, so a changed scenario does

62
00:04:01.088 --> 00:04:03.948
not depend on memorized wording.
